        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>Sergei Loznitsa likens removal of €2m grant to ‘a punishment in kindergarten’ on eve of Venice film festival</p><p>One of Ukraine’s most acclaimed film-makers has criticised the European Commission’s decision to cut off funds to the Venice Biennale over the opening of Russia’s pavilion, likening it to “a punishment in kindergarten”.</p><p>The <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/artanddesign/2026/may/05/venice-biennale-protests-resignations-russia-israel\">Biennale drew heavy criticism this spring</a> when it allowed Russia to use its pavilion for the first time since 2022, despite the ongoing full-scale invasion of Ukraine.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/film/2026/sep/02/ukrainian-film-maker-sergei-loznitsa-criticises-eu-cuts-venice-biennale-funding-russia-controversy\">Continue reading...</a>"
